From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dj <43033058+DjDeveloperr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:34:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] drm/apple: Add T6050 firmware-27 display support

Add T6050 firmware-27 display support, serialized IOMFB commands, paired scanout, register/clock metadata, and DisplayPort callbacks. Reuse the current AFK v2 codec, port the T6050 mapped callback-buffer behavior, and preserve the newer display-fabric and atomic-commit interfaces. This combines the old AFK and DCP PRs because the common framing implementation already exists in integration.

Source snapshot: t6050-gpu ee68abb105200e99636a5edfc647a5cfc1d89954
Integration base: 9cbdd0734d9e186c5f5f5949a21b909d10c2571b

Signed-off-by: Dj <43033058+DjDeveloperr@users.noreply.github.com>
[ J775D: backport onto integration/aurora: adapted to dcp.c, dcp_backlight.c, dptxep.c, iomfb.c, iomfb_internal.h, iomfb_template.c, parser.c, systemep.c and the dcp binding, alongside the newer desktop, panel and HDR paths; the pair's members, tiling record, lock and forget shared with the desktop 26.6 pair, so its forget now also runs on a 26.6 crash and at unbind; APIF selftests left out; comments reworded; code unchanged; original d977897ba23f ]
[ rebased onto integration/aurora: conflicts in iomfb_template.c and iomfb_v27.c only; the firmware-27 peer colour-matrix call now sits before the one set_matrix completion that "drm/apple: warn when the firmware refuses the colour matrix" introduced; the firmware-27 method table names A428 by its integration name, iomfbep_set_brightness_correction ("drm/apple: follow the colour matrix with identity brightness correction" renamed dcpep_pipe_set_428); otherwise unchanged; original 79634d7771c1 ]
Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>

(cherry picked from commit 2b564db1e5d3413d4324b0bb656e06cede494aba)
